# Recommended local model for HAI.
#
#   ollama create hai-qwen2.5 -f app/ollama/Modelfile
#   # then set LLM_MODEL=hai-qwen2.5
#
# Why a variant instead of using qwen2.5:14b directly: Ollama serves models with
# a 4096-token context by default, and HAI does not fit in it. The system prompt
# plus the three tool schemas are ~1,900 tokens before the user types anything,
# and every step of a tool loop re-sends the whole conversation. On overflow
# Ollama silently drops the oldest tokens — the system prompt goes first, and
# the model then loses its grounding and language rules mid-answer. Measured
# symptom: the same Sudan question answered in Thai with no tool call at 4096,
# and correctly in English with the right tool call at 16384.
#
# Baking num_ctx into a variant keeps this repeatable and leaves the shared
# Ollama server's own configuration alone. Setting OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=16384
# on the server instead works just as well.

FROM qwen2.5:14b

PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# HAI reports thresholds and figures; sampling variety buys nothing and costs
# tool-calling reliability. The chat route also sends temperature 0.
PARAMETER temperature 0
